{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>For YHWH will judge His people.</b> When He judges them with these sufferings that are stated upon them, as in ״כִּי בָם יָדִין עַמִּים״ (Job 36) — He disciplines nations. For this does not serve in the sense of 'because,' to give a reason for the words above, but is an expression of the beginning of a statement, as in (Leviticus 25) ״כִּי תָבֹאוּ אֶל הָאָרֶץ״ — when these judgments come upon them, the Holy One, blessed be He, will relent concerning His servants to turn back and have compassion upon them." "<b>He will relent.</b> An expression of a reversal of thought — for good or for ill." "<b>For He will see that the hand has slipped.</b> When He sees that the hand of the enemy grows and grows very strong against them — <b>and there is no</b> strength left in them, <b>shut up or at large</b>." "<b>Shut up.</b> Niphal — by means of a restrainer and ruler who restrains them." "<b>At large.</b> By means of one who leaves them unrestrained. עוֹצֵר is the ruler who restrains the people so that they do not go out dispersed when they go forth as an army against the enemy — בְּלַעַז מיינטינ״דור; <b>shut up</b> is the one restrained by the restraint of the ruler; <b>at large</b> — strong, as in (Nahum 3) ״וַיַּעַזְבוּ יְרוּשָׁלַיִם עַד הַחוֹמָה״; ״אֵיךְ לֹא עֻזְּבָה עִיר תְּהִלָּה״ (Jeremiah 49) — אינפורצדו״ר."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {4 "מיינטינ״דור = Old French maintiendor, 'one who maintains/restrains'; אינפורצדו״ר = Old French enforcedor, 'one who strengthens/fortifies'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:32.616551009Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}